From: Qt upstream, commit 1c6fb56a9686ad012b35ecbee9a67cc6686b6099
Subject: PipeWire callback lifetime and portal failure reporting

Backport of https://github.com/qt/qtmultimedia/commit/1c6fb56a9686ad012b35ecbee9a67cc6686b6099
Copyright (C) 2025 The Qt Company Ltd.
SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Qt-Commercial OR LGPL-3.0-only OR GPL-2.0-only OR GPL-3.0-only

Synchronize hook removal with PipeWire event-loop dispatch. Keep the native
Qt 6.10.2 ABI and system style plugins; do not replace the audio backend.

The first change is the upstream lifetime backport above. The second is an
AutoTalk correction: report unsuccessful portal responses through the existing
capture error interface after resetting request state. It does not repair KDE.

--- a/src/multimedia/pipewire/qpipewire_async_support.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/pipewire/qpipewire_async_support.cpp
@@ -84,3 +84,5 @@ CoreEventListener::~CoreEventListener()
 {
-    removeHooks();
+    QAudioContextManager::withEventLoopLock([&] {
+        removeHooks();
+    });
 }

--- a/src/multimedia/pipewire/qpipewire_screencapturehelper.cpp
+++ b/src/multimedia/pipewire/qpipewire_screencapturehelper.cpp
@@ -140,6 +140,7 @@ void QPipeWireCaptureHelper::gotRequestResponse(uint result, const QVariantMap &map)
     if (result != 0) {
         m_operationState = NoOperation;
-        qWarning() << "Failed to capture screen via pipewire, perhaps because user cancelled the operation.";
         m_requestToken = -1;
+        updateError(QPlatformSurfaceCapture::InternalError,
+                    result == 1 ? u"Screen sharing was cancelled."_s : u"The screen-sharing service could not start capture."_s);
         return;
     }
